{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/LINQ Query Provider.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/LINQ Query Provider.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"linq query provider linq query provider","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/LINQ Query Provider.md","fileName":"LINQ Query Provider.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"LINQ Query Provider","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 21:16\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[LINQ Query Construction]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["LINQ Query Construction","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/LINQ Query Provider.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/LINQ Query Provider.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"linq query provider linq query provider","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/LINQ Query Provider.md","fileName":"LINQ Query Provider.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"LINQ Query Provider","heading":"LINQ Query Provider","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A LINQ query provider interprets a query expression for a particular data source. In-memory sequences execute delegates through `IEnumerable<T>`, while `IQueryable<T>` providers inspect expression trees and may translate them into SQL or another remote query language.\n\nThis distinction explains why not every .NET method can be used in a database query and why execution behavior varies by source. Provider-backed queries should be evaluated for their generated operations, not assumed to behave like ordinary in-memory loops.","tags":["baby"],"links":["LINQ Query Construction","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/LINQ Query Provider.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/LINQ Query Provider.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__n